item.description:
I've always believed that some of the best conversations happen when you're willing to slow down and really listen. And that's exactly what happened when I sat down with Grammy Award-winning artist Amy Grant.

Amy opens up about some of the hardest chapters of her life, from navigating divorce and criticism to overcoming fear and learning to trust her own voice again after throat surgery. We also talk about her 26-year marriage to Vince Gill, how they've learned to communicate through disagreements, and why accepting the person in front of you can change everything about your relationship.

Listen to Amy’s new album, The Me That Remains:

https://open.spotify.com/album/40Q1PUv4aWPsxGJTvlKHx4&nbsp;

Join me on Supercast for ad-free episodes, bonus content, and AMAs: https://jefferson.supercast.com/

