item.description:
Inner peace isn't about having everything in your life go perfectly. It's about learning how to stay grounded when things don't. In this episode, I sit down with bestselling author Yung Pueblo (Diego Perez) to talk about how self-awareness, meditation, and letting go can completely change the way we communicate and connect with others. We discuss how our past shapes our reactions, how to stay calm during difficult conversations, and why learning to pause before responding might be one of the most powerful skills you can develop. Diego also shares what he learned from spending 60 days in complete silence and how we can all find more peace without needing to change everything around us.

Buy Diego’s new book, Journey: The Year That Changes Everything: https://yungpueblo.com/journey&nbsp;

